174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 366 0 R
/ActualText (Reliability of feature importance scores: Feature importance scores quantify the extent to which a model relies on a feature to make predictions. They do not necessarily quantify the contribution of a feature to the overall accuracy of a model \(i.e. the feature's usefulness\). This is a subtle but fundamental difference, that shows RFECV won't magically fix a poor base model. Prior to inspecting the feature importances, it is important to check that the model predictive performance is high enough as there would be little interest of inspecting the important features of a non-predictive model.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 367 0 R
/ActualText (Drawbacks of RFECV: The limitations of RFECV stem from the limitations of the feature importance measures it relies on. For instance, decision trees, which are often used in feature importance calculations, struggle with high cardinality features.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 112 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
