/T (NOTES ON RFECV )
/E (NOTES ON RFECV )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 368 0 R
/ActualText (How to handle multicollinear/correlated features: The RFECV technique can handle correlated features but does not necessarily eliminate highly correlated features, since we have seen it be able to select highly correlated variables too. Instead, we should take caution about how well suited your model is to handling highly correlated variables, i.e. if your base model can handle correlated features, then RFECV itself will likely not present any problems either. If your model requires less degree of multicolliniearity in the data, consider applying another dimensionality reduction technique such as PCA before using RFECV. PCA removes the highly correlated features from the dataset and makes RFECV more reliable as a second feature selection layer.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
